    "text": "the FORM - XXV pointing out the non-compliance of provisions of safety, health and working conditions under the Code or rules or regulations or standards made there under, to the employer or occupier or manager or owner or master or officer-in-charge of the ship or their agent. (2) An Inspector -cum-Facilitator shall at each inspection, ascertain to what extent any shortcomings notified at a previous inspection have been rectified and the notices previously issued have been complied with and their findings and any shortcomings whi ch may come to light during the inspection, together with any order passed by them under the Code or rule or the regulations or standards made thereunder shall be recorded and maintained. 79. Powers and Duties of District Magistrate. - Powers and duties of District Magistrate in respect of mines, will be specified by general or special order by the Central Government issued from time to time. 196 THE GAZETTE OF INDIA : EXTRAORDINARY [PART II—SEC. 3(i)] 80. Qu",
