    "text": "he establishments, shall be complied with. 84. Adequate safety of employment of women in dangerous operations.- The Central Government may declare from time to time by notification, the class of establishments and the standard for safeguarding of women employed in hazardous processes as specified in the First Schedule to the Code. 198 THE GAZETTE OF INDIA : EXTRAORDINARY [PART II—SEC. 3(i)] CHAPTER XI PART I CONTRACT LABOUR 85. Qualification and criteria of the contractor.- For the purposes of obtaining license, the contractor as an entity or as an individual shall not be an un -discharged insolvent or be convicted at any time during the last two years, of an offence which is liable for punishment for more than three months of imprisonment. 86. Conditions of License.- (1) The contractor shall ensure that:- (i) the hours of work shall conform to rules relating to section 25 of the Code; (ii) the wages shall be paid in accordance with the Code on Wages, 2019 (29 of 2019); (iii) if the co",
