    "text": "deposit, shall be deposited, if number of contract labour increases. 97. Appeal. – (1) The appellate authority under sub-section (1) of section 52 of the Code shall be notified by the Central Government, issued from time to time. (2) The form and the fees for this purpose will be specified by general or special order by Central Government issued from time to time. 98. Responsibility of payment of wages.- (1) The contractor shall fix the wage periods in respect of which wages shall be payable and no wage period shall exceed one month. (2) The wages of every person employed as contract labour in an establishment or by a contractor shall be paid before the expiry of seventh day after the last day of the wage period in respect of which the wages are payable. (3) The principal employer shall settle the bills of contractor related to dues of contract worker within timeline as per the terms and conditions agreed between principal employer and contractor. (4) The wages shall be disbursed thro",
