    "text": "असाधारण 213 (a) the total number of persons ordinarily employed in below ground workings of all such mines does not exceed 5000; and (b) the mines are situated within radius of 35 kms from and connected by road with the rescue room : Provided further that the Chief Inspector-cum-Facilitator may permit the employer of a group of mines having the total number of persons ordinarily employed below ground in excess of 5000 to use the rescue room as a rescue station excepting the functions o f imparting initial training in rescue work, if such rescue room is .- (i) equipped with requisite additional rescue apparatus including at least 15 extra sets of two hour self- contained breathing apparatus; and (ii) placed under the charge of a person holding the qualifications, experience and like other requirements of instructors and minimum of five rescue trained persons of whom at least one shall hold the qualifications, experience and like other requirements of rescue room in-charge are posted the",
