    "text": "be specified by the Chief Inspector -cum-Facilitator through general or special order issued from time to time and shall be maintained at the entrance of such mine. (3) Self- contained breathing apparatus shall be provided at a rescue station and that at rescue rooms under it shall be of the same type and make. (4) The following apparatus and equipments provided under of sub -rules (1),(2) and (3), shall be of a type or standard approved by the Chief Inspector-cum-Facilitator, namely:- (a) breathing apparatus; (b) smoke helmets, tube apparatus and apparatus serving the same purpose; (c) reviving apparatus; (d) electric safety lamps and flame safety lamps; (e) gas detector; and (f) self-rescuers. (5) All breathing apparatus and every flow meter shall be adjusted and tested and the purity of oxygen for use in breathing apparatus shall be tested in such manners as may be specified by the Chief Inspector-cum-Facilitator through general or special order issued from time to time. (6) In eve",
