    "text": "section ( 1) of section 115 for the unorganised workers. (5) Nothing contained in sub-section ( 1) shall apply to a penalty or an offence committed by a person for a second or subsequent time within a period of three years from the date of penalty or offence, as the case may be,— (a) which was earlier compounded; or (b) for which such person was earlier convicted. CHAPTER XIII S OCIAL SECURITY FUND 115. (1) There shall be established by the appropriate Government a social security fund for the welfare of the unorganised workers to which there shall be credited the amount received from composition of the offence as specified in sub-section (4) of section 114 and the amount of the penalty as specified in sub-section ( 6) of section 111. (2) The fund may also be funded by such other sources as may be prescribed by the appropriate Government. (3) The fund shall be administered and expended for welfare of the unorganised workers in such manner as may be prescribed by the appropriate Governm",
